  "notes": "The aft sweep, fin, engines and winglets are the ones measured from photos for the oneworld scheme (N486AS/N487AS), checked here against N928AK and N963AK (2025). The title's place and size are from a climbing, tilted view (N928AK) and approximate. Hawaiian (HAL) keeps its own scheme under the Alaska Air Group. Alaska's 787-9s (ex-Hawaiian order, from January 2026) wear a separate 'global' livery (ASA/global). The title's length (0.19) was measured on Alaska's side-on photo of N710AL, which wears the standard title. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N298AK (737-900ER, Jan 2024) and N928AK (737-9, June 2025), drawn on the 737-900ER (the commonest type, the -9 the same length): the title runs from just behind the forward door (x 0.16, the A's long crossbar) to 0.37 on both photos, so it starts a little aft and runs longer than first drawn; its lowercase is about 0.55 of the capital A's height; its baseline sits about 1.6 m under the windows, as drawn. The aft sweep's front edge probed within 0.4 m of the drawing; its four edges made smooth curves. On a 737-800 (about 2.6 m shorter) the title sits a little further aft as a share of the length. A narrow silver-grey stripe runs just ahead of the lime (sharp-edged on N298AK, N928AK and the E175s, in sun and shade): added under the lime, its front edge about 0.5 m ahead of the lime's, measured relative to the lime because the photos are from below.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2016 livery replaced the 1990 scheme (Native face, blue 'Alaska' in a different script with a blue-green stripe); the merged Virgin America fleet took it from 2018.",
  "types": {
    "B789": {
      "note": "Alaska's 787-9s wear the widebody 'global' (aurora) livery, not this one: drawn in full as ASA/global (the same paint, copied here so a 787 flying as ASA that isn't tagged yet still gets it). Measured on N782HA (Commons, 2026-04-23) and Alaska's press photos of N784HA. No Native face on the tail: the logos list is empty. Keep this entry and ASA/global the same.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "sourceRefs": [
        6
      ],
